From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 22 Aug 2026 04:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] sky1: guard missing NPU core platform devices

sky1_npu_probe() looks up each ACPI CRE core child with
bus_find_device_by_fwnode(&platform_bus_type, child) and then calls
pm_runtime_enable() / dev_pm_domain_attach() / dev_pm_set_driver_flags()
/ ACPI_COMPANION()->... on the result UNCONDITIONALLY.

On the Minisforum MS-R1 the factory BIOS's DSDT contains the
\_SB.NPU0.CRE0-2 Device objects but omits their _HID ("CIXH4010"), so
Linux creates acpi_device nodes (device:0c-0e) but never creates
platform devices for them.  Unless the NCZ NPUCRE SSDT override
(assets/npu/ssdt-npucre.asl, injected as an initrd early-CPIO) is
loaded, the lookup returns NULL and pm_runtime_enable(NULL) faults on
spin_lock_irqsave(&dev->power.lock) -- a NULL dereference at
offsetof(struct device, power.lock) (0xcc/0xec depending on kernel
layout), PC in _raw_spin_lock_irqsave, called straight from the probe
path:

  Unable to handle kernel NULL pointer dereference at virtual address 00000000000000cc
  pc : _raw_spin_lock_irqsave+0x2c/0x50
  ... sky1 probe -> platform_probe -> really_probe -> ... -> aipu_init

With oops=panic this takes down every boot of an MS-R1 whose initrd
lacks the SSDT override (any update-initramfs regeneration strips the
prepended early-CPIO, and ISOs built without assets/npu staged never
had it).  Verified live on MS-R1 (cixmini, BIOS 1.0 03/12/2026):
CIXH4000:00 enumerates, zero CIXH4010 platform devices exist; the same
kernel boots clean with aipu blacklisted.  On the Radxa Orion O6N the
firmware provides _HID natively (CIXH4010:00-02 platform devices
present) which is why this never reproduced there.

Skip cores whose platform device is missing, and fail the probe with
-ENODEV when fewer than CIX_NPU_PD_NUM cores are usable: with cores
unpowered the TSM accepts jobs that never complete (pool BUSY, no IRQ),
so probing "successfully" would only trade the panic for a wedge.  The
KMD 1.0 tree (assets/kernel/npu/src) already carried an equivalent
IS_ERR_OR_NULL guard; the switch to the vendor 6.2.0 stack regressed it.

Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
---
--- a/driver/armchina-npu/sky1/sky1.c	2026-08-22 03:39:32.898597090 +0000
+++ b/driver/armchina-npu/sky1/sky1.c	2026-08-22 03:39:50.768115250 +0000
@@ -555,6 +555,24 @@
 					break;
 
 				cix_aipu_priv->pd_core[i] = bus_find_device_by_fwnode(&platform_bus_type, child);
+				if (IS_ERR_OR_NULL(cix_aipu_priv->pd_core[i])) {
+					/*
+					 * The CRE core exists in the ACPI
+					 * namespace but has no platform device:
+					 * firmware omits _HID "CIXH4010" (e.g.
+					 * Minisforum MS-R1 BIOS 1.0) and the
+					 * NPUCRE SSDT override is not loaded.
+					 * Without this check the unconditional
+					 * pm_runtime_enable(NULL) below oopses in
+					 * _raw_spin_lock_irqsave on
+					 * &NULL->power.lock and panics the boot.
+					 */
+					dev_err(&p_dev->dev,
+						"NPU core %s has no platform device (firmware omits _HID; NPUCRE SSDT override not loaded)\n",
+						acpi_device_bid(to_acpi_device_node(child)));
+					cix_aipu_priv->pd_core[i] = NULL;
+					continue;
+				}
 				if (cix_aipu_priv->pd_core[i]) {
 					struct device *core = cix_aipu_priv->pd_core[i];
 
@@ -587,6 +605,20 @@
                 i++;
             }
         }
+		if (i < CIX_NPU_PD_NUM) {
+			/*
+			 * Fewer usable cores than the hardware is supposed to
+			 * have: the NPU cannot be powered correctly, and
+			 * proceeding wedges every dispatched job (pool BUSY,
+			 * no completion IRQ). Fail the probe cleanly -- a
+			 * missing NPU beats an unbootable or wedged system.
+			 */
+			dev_err(&p_dev->dev,
+				"only %d of %d NPU cores usable - disabling NPU\n",
+				i, CIX_NPU_PD_NUM);
+			sky1_npu_teardown_cores(&p_dev->dev);
+			return -ENODEV;
+		}
 #endif
     } else {
 		ret = sky1_npu_attach_pd(&p_dev->dev, &sky1);
